        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0672" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v28/pg640"/>

                <head>323. Memorandum From Secretary of Defense McNamara to the Chairman of the
                    Joint Chiefs of Staff (Wheeler)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d323-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1967-12-18">December 18, 1967</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>The Use of Propeller and Jet Aircraft in Laos</item>
                </list>
                <p>The enclosed study indicates that propeller aircraft are approximately 9 times as
                    effective as jet aircraft per sortie in destroying trucks and water craft in
                    Laos. It appears possible to substitute two A–1 squadrons for two F–4 squadrons
                    in Thailand and significantly increase the effectiveness <pb facs="0673" n="641"
                        xml:id="pg641"/> of our air interdiction campaign in the Laotian Panhandle
                    without reducing the number of jet sorties in North Vietnam.</p>
                <p>Would you please review the enclosed study and give me your recommendations by
                    December 29, 1967.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d323-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold"> Robert S. McNamara </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d323-a1.xml" xpointer="d323-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
